Hoi Lena,

As promised on the phone last night, here it is in writing so you have it for Pieter and for the file. Sorry it didn't =
make 15:00 yesterday, I was on a roof in Botlek with no signal most of the afternoon.

February first, because you asked and because it was my visit.

I did the February call-out (00041055). L-03 on circuit 2 after the winter restart, suction 2.1 bar. I worked to KT-WI-=
14: visual inspection of circuit 2, the joints, service valves and around the compressor, no oil traces, no leak found.=
 The deficit came out under 10% of nameplate charge, so per KT-WI-14 I topped up 2.5 kg R-513A and left it running to m=
onitor. That is what the work instruction says, and it's how we did it at Kyltek for years. KT-WI-14 also says to sched=
ule a full leak test at the next planned visit. I can't find in Servio or Salesforce that it was ever scheduled. I shou=
ld have made sure it was.

What I didn't do: I did not check the EXV campaign. RTM-H-0007 is serial NK600-230415. That is inside the serial range =
of the Nordkyl bulletin SB-2025-014 (NK600-220001 up to NK600-231999), campaign NK-C25-14. The symptom in the bulletin =
is L-03 after idle periods with normal charge, because the expansion valve sticks. A winter restart is exactly an idle =
period. So your memory is right, and it is quite possible the February alarm was the valve and not the charge at all, a=
nd I put 2.5 kg into a circuit that didn't need it. I'll check for that too.

Eerlijk gezegd, the worst part is that I put the campaign warning on the EU chiller field guide myself last October. I =
didn't connect it on the day. Balen.

I've checked what we have. No record of the campaign being done on 0007. RTM-H-0008 is NK600-240702, outside the range,=
 so that one is fine. GDN-H-0014 in Gdansk is NK600-221190, also inside the range, but that one Jakub and I did last Oc=
tober. That is the unit that taught us about the valve in the first place, which makes missing it on 0007 worse.

Who goes: me. Jakub can't, he isn't F-gas certified yet, and he did the right thing on Monday by not putting gauges on =
it. I can be on site Thursday 1 October at 07:00. Jakub has asked Pieter's shift lead for roof access and the work at h=
eight permit for Thursday morning. I'll take Jakub with me so he sees it done.

Plan on site:
1. Check the EXV on circuit 2 first, before anything is connected to the refrigerant side: valve position in the servic=
e menu at restart and under load, superheat, and whether it's modulating or stuck. Also check which valve is fitted, re=
v 2 or rev 3. The label is readable on that unit.
2. If it's the valve: replace with 63-1180 rev 3 on both circuits as the campaign says, booked under NK-C25-14. I email=
ed Mette Kjaer at Nordkyl this morning to confirm 0007 is still open on their campaign list and to get two valves sent =
to Rotterdam. If they're not here by Thursday, I do the diagnosis Thursday and come back for the swap.
3. If the valve is fine, or the charge is still short after the valve: leak test per SOP-020 and repair. No top-up. If =
I can't find the leak, I tag the unit and escalate, which is what SOP-020 says to do.
4. Either way I recover and weigh what's in circuit 2, so we know what the February 2.5 kg actually did.

For Pieter, I would say: in February we followed an instruction that allowed a top-up without a leak test; we missed a =
manufacturer campaign on the expansion valve that matches his symptoms; a certified engineer (me) is there Thursday at =
07:00; we will not top up; and he gets the root cause in writing after the visit. I would not promise him it's the valv=
e until I've seen it.

One more thing, and I'd like you to take it up because I can't. KT-WI-14 and SOP-020 say opposite things. SOP-020 says =
never top up without a leak test, and check the bulletins for the serial first. KT-WI-14, my own instruction from 2021,=
 says top up if there's no visible leak and the deficit is under 10%. Both are in SharePoint, both look valid, and FS-S=
TD-001 says the Kyltek instructions stay valid until superseded without saying which ones. So a technician here can do =
exactly what I did in February and be following procedure. I wrote KT-WI-14, but I don't own it any more. It was migrat=
ed in 2024 and nobody took it over. Who owns retiring it? Rachel? I'm happy to do the work, but someone on the Corvane =
side has to sign it off, otherwise this happens again on the next NK-600 after a cold week.

Groetjes,
Sofie

Sofie de Vries
